  "notes": "The project install fails on both sides (setuptools rejects the flat layout), so only the needed dependencies were installed into both venvs (claude-agent-sdk, python-dotenv, pydantic, secretstorage, coverage), and the source tree is added to sys.path. The workload runs ParallelOrchestratorReviewer.review() end to end on 150 seeded PRs. Stand-ins replace only external I/O: create_client (Claude SDK, which answers through the real process_sdk_stream) and GHClient (gh CLI). Changed lines are 100% covered on both sides. Outputs differ as expected: head keeps validator-dismissed findings as 'disputed' (shown in the summary but excluded from the verdict) and keeps cross-validated findings, where base drops dismissed findings. Every run ends in the BLOCKED verdict. The concurrency is asyncio.gather inside one process (no threads or processes)."
